FineWine: acceleration structure host commands, serialization and size queries

Completes VK_KHR_acceleration_structure on top of 0001.

- Host commands (vkBuildAccelerationStructuresKHR, vkCopyAccelerationStructureKHR,
  vkCopyAccelerationStructureToMemoryKHR, vkCopyMemoryToAccelerationStructureKHR,
  vkWriteAccelerationStructuresPropertiesKHR). Metal builds on the GPU only, so each records
  the same work in a Metal command buffer of MoltenVK's own and waits for it. Inputs given as
  host pointers are copied into Metal buffers. accelerationStructureHostCommands is reported.
- Query pools for VK_QUERY_TYPE_ACCELERATION_STRUCTURE_COMPACTED_SIZE_KHR (written by the GPU)
  and ..._SERIALIZATION_SIZE_KHR, and vkCmdWriteAccelerationStructuresPropertiesKHR.
- Serialization. Metal cannot write an acceleration structure out or read one in. What is
  written after Vulkan's header is what the structure was built from, and reading it back
  builds it again. Every structure therefore remembers its last build's Metal descriptor.
- vkGetDeviceAccelerationStructureCompatibilityKHR compares the header's two UUIDs.

